WEBVTT

open
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
One plan hits its limit. The others sit unused.

title
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.600
Excalibur. Keep coding when one subscription hits its limit.

step-1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.000
One thread. Type a task once. xcb picks the project and the account.

step-2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.400
Quota that resets first. The account whose unused quota is closest to lapsing gets the task.

step-3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.800
Moves on at a limit. A limit mid-task? xcb continues it on another account.

step-4
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.200
Runs in the background. Close the terminal. xcb attention shows what needs you.

step-5
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.100
From any machine. Send a task from your laptop to the desktop at home.

proof
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.600
3 providers: Claude, Codex, Devin. 5 min longest a usage reading counts

limits
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.600
What it doesn't do. xcb doesn't raise any usage limit. It spends the quota you already have, in a better order.

end
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.100
Excalibur. xcb.sh. Free for macOS and Linux. Latest release: v0.12.0.
